# Platform docs consistency

When creating or updating documentation in this multi-root workspace, consult the relevant platform docs and match the **host document's** structure, widgets, heading style, and tone.

## Primary platform docs

| Topic | Where to read first |
| :--- | :--- |
| ParaDOCS plugin | `docs/ParaDOCS-Plugin-Overview.md` (includes Changelog), `docs/paradocs-plugin-notes.md` |
| Paragon Knowledge | `docs/Paragon-Knowledge-MCP-Overview.md` (includes Changelog) |
| Cursor platform (canonical) | `cursor-test`: `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` (including §2 HITL morning checklist), pages under `user-guide/` and `admin-guide/` you touch, `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-Changelog.md` |
| Markdown style | Bundled `docs/Paragon_Markdown_Style_Rules.md` (plugin) or canonical `cursor-test/Paragon_Markdown_Style_Rules.md` |
| ParaDOCS convert app | Technical Documentation `CHANGELOG.md`, `paradocs.py`, related settings docs |

## "Consider" means

Before claiming documentation work is done:

1. Check whether companion pages need a factual update for the same change.
2. If yes, edit them in the same task (surgical edits, not parallel doc trees).
3. **Trim stale content** in the same task: anything superseded, replaced, or no longer relevant (see `trim-stale-docs.mdc`). Do not only append.
4. Do **not** require rewriting every corpus `.md` (tech-arch / abbey-view) unless the change is about those corpora.

## Match host format and tone

1. Read the target file and a neighbouring section or sibling page before drafting.
2. Reuse that page's patterns: numbered H2s, ADO wiki widgets, tables, callout style, operator reference vs second-person guide voice.
3. Follow Paragon Markdown style and plugin overlays (no em dashes, no third-person Paragon actor in guides).
4. Do not impose User Guide procedure-box HTML on plain operator docs (overview, changelog), or flatten wiki widgets into bare Markdown when editing guides.
5. Prefer surgical edits over wholesale rewrites. Keep existing heading hierarchy and column layouts. When new facts replace old ones, **delete or shorten** the old text rather than stacking both.

## HITL morning checklist

When an edit changes how operators run morning checks (Michu, Trundle, CI, Security Agents, Automations, changelog Summary, vendor links, plugin MCP Connected, Admin Dashboard glance), update `cursor-test` `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md` §2 in the same task. See `hitl-morning-checklist-sync.mdc`.

## Changelog routing

After doc edits, route changelog rows per `changelog-ownership.mdc`. Do not duplicate history across repos.

## Kanban (Paragon Docs roadmap)

When work maps to roadmap cards on `cursor-test`, follow `kanban-board-sync.mdc`. Ask before creating a new card for an uncovered task.

## Out of scope

- Inventing parallel operator docs when an existing page already covers the topic.
- Editing the ADO mirror for content that lives on GitLab `cursor-test`.
- Style-only rewrites with no factual change (see Michu / Trundle guardrails on `cursor-test`).
